iFixit today tore down the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/apple-homeview/">Apple HomeView</a> to see what's inside, and found that the device takes a step backward in repairability compared to the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/homepod/">HomePod</a>. Getting into it resulted in damage to internal components.<br/>
<br/>
<div class="center-wrap"><iframe title="Apple Was Getting Better. Then We Opened This." src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/rr7m9nBqDdo" width="560" height="315" frameborder="0" allowfullscreen="allowfullscreen"></iframe></div><br/>
Strong adhesive holds the HomeView's display in place, and iFixit said it was difficult to remove. There's a mix of Phillips and Torx screws in different sizes securing internal components, necessitating several tools.<br/>
<br/>
Speakers take up most of the internal space behind the display, with the logic board located behind them. The logic board has a shield that connects to the back of the aluminum enclosure, turning the entire thing into a heat sink to improve thermal performance. The thermal paste and adhesive attaching the shield to the casing made the logic board difficult to remove.<br/>
<br/>
The speakers are held in place with a thick adhesive pad, and attempting to remove one caused it to snap in half. There are multiple cables connecting the display to the speaker base, and iFixit found the components of the wall-mounted and tabletop versions of the HomeView aren't interchangeable. The devices have different internal designs, with the wall-mounted version using a larger logic board and the tabletop model adopting larger speakers and a pivot mount.<br/>
<br/>
The HomeView speaker base is designed similarly to a &zwnj;HomePod&zwnj;, and iFixit found it easier to take apart. The USB-C port on the base is modular and can be replaced, as can the two passive speakers inside the enclosure. Because of how the HomeView is assembled, it isn't possible to separate the display from the base without going through the display side.<br/>
<br/>
